<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50174" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθᾱγενής</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span></span>, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθαιγ-</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			14.203
		</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			2.17
		</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pers.</u>
			306
		</span></i>(v.l.), <i><span class="en">
			Alex.Aet.
		</span></i> (v. infr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>born in lawful wedlock</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλά
				με</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶσον ἰθαγενέεσσιν</span> (so most codd.
			and <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				187.24
			</span></i>: 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθαιγ-</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἐτίμα</span> honoured me
				like
			<i>his true-born sons</i>, of a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόθος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				12.2
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθαγ-</span> cod.), <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aet.
				3.2
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθαιγ-</span> cod.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a nation, <i>from
				the ancient stock, aboriginal</i>, opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπηλυς, ἰ. Αἰγύπτιοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.53
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				306
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχ ὑπ᾽ ἰθαγενῶν ἤρχοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					7.7.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				2.15
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. κύημα</span>, opp. an abortion, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.71
			</span></i>; of some mouths of the Nile, <i>natural, original</i>,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρυκτά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. νότος, ζέφυρος</span>,
				<i>genuine</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				364a16
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i>. (Glossed <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτόχθων</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐθιγενής</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>; <i>originalis, indigena</i>, by <u>Gloss.</u>;
			perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθᾰ-γενής [ᾱ</span> metri gr.],
			cf. Skt. <i>ihá</i>, Avest. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδα</span> (fr. <i>*idhá</i>) 'here'; cf. pr.
			n. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰθαγένης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Per.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				<u>Vit.Hom.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰθαιγένης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(9).192
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
